1. Install a python version that works with pygame, use python versions below 3.14
2. Install .venv with requirements.txt, In vs studio its 'Ctrl Shift P' then python > create environment
3. Run in terminal 'python -m game.main' from the root folder

This version has got core down so that we can make multiple levels, all thats left is to create the elements to work with our future story

To make 'new levels' use the base class from  environments/base.py, the setup and loop in there are called in window/display.py, Look at level1.py/level2.py for better representation of how to setup new levels
You can get available gui elements from window/ui.py but rn theres only a button implemented
In the setup function you want to initialize everything you want on the scene, and in the update function there are things that are interacted with through the user that needs updateing. 

Obviously if you don't like some things feel free to change it cause this is just my way of thinking how to implement our game so far

